    {
      "id": "lem:observable-cubic-reduction",
      "proposed": {
        "tex_ref": "observable-proposed"
      },
      "reason": "The original converse omitted the necessary condition \\(l(\\alpha)\\neq0\\). Replace the five exponential sources in the displayed legal witness by independent centered Laplace sources: the same source-support factorization verifies independence genericity, its covariance still has \\(v\\chi\\neq0\\), and central symmetry gives \\(T_3=0\\). Both observable cubics then vanish identically, so their denominator root is a cubic common root but cannot solve \\(F_{11}=0\\). The narrowed statement is exactly reversible and remains sufficient for the \\(D\\neq0\\) singleton theorem.",
      "direction": "narrow"
    }
